---

## Root Cause

The TLS certificate used for Auth Service to connect to Users Database expired at 14:23 UTC. The certificate had a 1-year validity and was not included in our certificate monitoring system. When the certificate expired, Auth Service could no longer establish connections to Users Database, causing all authentication requests to fail.

---

## Contributing Factors

1. Certificate was manually provisioned outside standard process
2. No monitoring for certificate expiration on internal services
3. Auth Service had no fallback for database connection failures
4. Blast radius was large due to synchronous dependency pattern

---

## Lessons Learned

**What went well:**
- On-call response was fast (3 minutes to acknowledge)
- Root cause was identified within 10 minutes
- Clear runbook existed for certificate rotation

**What went poorly:**
- No advance warning of certificate expiration
- All services failed simultaneously due to Auth dependency
- No cached authentication possible during outage

